 "journal": [
  {
   "day": 1,
   "text": "First proper day ashore, and I'm writing this by firelight with bracken up to my knees. Got the frame of a lean-to up and a ring of stones round the fire, and tonight, God willing, I won't freeze for it. Cut my hand on something in the wreckage this morning — nothing that won't mend. Tired in a way I don't think sleep alone will fix, but the fire's caught and holding, and that's the whole of my luck today and I'll take it. Tomorrow: the roof, before the weather remembers where it left off."
  }
 ],
 "lastThought": "Fire's caught proper now, and there's a roof half over my head. First day nearly done and I'm still breathing — that'll do for a start."
